course: dictionary
lesson: 5794
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and mace is one of them. You cannot know which meaning is right from the word alone, so read the context: the words and sentences around it. «The Cossack fought with a spiked bulava mace.» The clue is spiked, and fought: here a mace is a weapon, a heavy club.
explain: The same word can mean something quite different in another place. In a parliament, the mace is a decorated staff. It is placed on the table while the House is sitting, to show that Parliament is meeting. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In a kitchen, a pinch of mace is a spice, made from the red covering of the nutmeg seed, and it goes into cakes and sauces. The clue is pinch, and the kitchen words around it. Mace can also be a stinging spray, but a sentence about a spray or police will tell you that.
fact: Mace has several meanings: a club, a ceremonial staff, a spice, and a stinging spray.
fact: A mace as a weapon is a heavy club with a metal head, often with spikes, used by knights in the Middle Ages.
fact: A mace as a ceremony object is a decorated staff that shows the power of a mayor, parliament or university.
fact: Mace as a spice is made from the red covering of the nutmeg seed.
fact: Mace is also a brand name of a spray that stings the eyes, often used by some police in the US.
exercise: «The knight swung his spiked mace at the enemy.» What is a mace in this sentence? | A stick for walking | *A heavy club with a metal head | A decorated bag | A spice for cakes
exercise: «The mace was placed on the table as the House sat.» What does the mace show? | *That Parliament is meeting | That the cake needs more spice | That it is time for lunch | That the knights are coming
exercise: «Add a pinch of mace to the sauce.» What is mace in this sentence? | *A spice | A weapon | A stinging spray | A ceremonial staff
test: «The Cossack carried a bulava mace into battle.» In this sentence, mace means | A flower | A brand of spray | *A heavy club used as a weapon | A spice for cooking
test: «Mace is a warm spice that goes well in cakes.» In this sentence, mace means | A weapon of knights | A decorated staff | A spray for the eyes | *A kind of spice, made from nutmeg
exam: In «The mayor carried the ceremonial mace through the hall», which word tells you mace is a decorated staff, not a weapon? | through | *ceremonial | hall | carried
